{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Alan Faena (Buenos Aires, November 20, 1963) is an Argentine hotelier and real estate developer.","title":"Alan Faena"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He has developed properties in Miami Beach, Florida and Buenos Aires, Argentina.","title":"Alan Faena"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Faena is the founder and President of the Faena Group.","title":"Alan Faena"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" He is a member of the Tate International Committee and the New Museum Leaders Council.","title":"Alan Faena"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" He previously founded Via Vai in 1985, a fashion label, and worked as a fashion designer.","title":"Alan Faena"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Disco Ruined My Life, also known as DRML, is a fashion label created by Maurice Uzzan, award winning designer from Graniph Designs  based in Rome, Italy.","title":"Disco Ruined My Life"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" DRML is a fashion label that showcases "high fashion" icons such as Comme des Garçons, Hermès, Givenchy, Yves Saint Laurent and Alexander McQueen with ironic symbols.","title":"Disco Ruined My Life"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Many of the designs consist of the original logo, however, changed to give a different meaning while still recognizable.","title":"Disco Ruined My Life"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Wertheim Performing Arts Center (also known by the abbreviation WPAC, full name The Herbert and Nicole Wertheim Performing Arts Center) is a performing arts center that opened in 1996.","title":"Wertheim Performing Arts Center"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Situated in the downtown Miami campus of Florida International University (FIU), it is named after Dr. Herbert Wertheim, an inventor, engineer, scientist, educator, clinician, entrepreneur, philanthropist and community leader, founder and president of Brain Power Incorporated and his wife Nicole Wertheim.","title":"Wertheim Performing Arts Center"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Both were heavily involved in development of the university.","title":"Wertheim Performing Arts Center"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Ximena Caminos is Chair of Faena Art, Executive Creative Director and partner in Faena Group, and Chief Curator and Executive Director of the Faena Arts Center in Buenos Aires since 2004.","title":"Ximena Caminos"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Caminos leads the Faena Prize for the Arts (see: Faena Arts Center), one of the largest art prizes in Latin America.","title":"Ximena Caminos"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Caminos is the Executive Director of Faena Forum, "a new kind of multidisciplinary center in a flexible building that can house dance, theater, political debates, lectures and a wide range of other cultural happenings," opened in Miami Beach in 2016 and designed by Rem Koolhaas","title":"Ximena Caminos"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Faena Art Center is the cultural center of the Faena District Buenos Aires, a residential and cultural community in the Puerto Madero waterfront in Buenos Aires developed by the Faena Group and opened in September 2011.","title":"Faena Arts Center"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Alan Faena founded the center.","title":"Faena Arts Center"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Ximena Caminos is the Executive Director.","title":"Faena Arts Center"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Austin School of Film, also known as the The Austin School of Film @ Motion Media Arts Center, is an art, film and technology institute through non-profit, Motion Media Arts Center and is located on Tillery Street in Austin, Texas.","title":"Austin School of Film"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The Austin School of Film began its start in 2002 under the non-profit umbrella name of Motion Media Arts Center and by merging of the Austin Cinemaker Co-op (founded 1996) and the Center for Young Cinema (founded 1999).","title":"Austin School of Film"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The goal of the school is to educate, train, and develop emerging artists of all ages to be active participants in shaping our culture.","title":"Austin School of Film"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The organization's program spans the entire spectrum of art, film and tech offering a range of classes from filmmaking, coding, web and graphic design, animation, digital media arts production to software training and apple certification.","title":"Austin School of Film"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" They also offer certificate programs such as Digital Video Certificate Program, to help students develop technical skills in production and post-production and complete a series of courses to develop a filmmaking knowledge base.","title":"Austin School of Film"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Via Vai
